menu "Remote options"

config PROVISIONING_HEADER_DIR
	string "Directory containing this unit's generated provisioning_data.h"
	help
	  Generated by dongle/tools/provision.py — PLAN.md §4's binding
	  decision, 2026-08-12: identity is baked into the image at build
	  time, not read from a flash partition written by a separate step.
	  Same reasoning as dongle/Kconfig's identical option: this has to be
	  a Kconfig string, not a plain CMake -D variable, because west build
	  runs under sysbuild and only CONFIG_-prefixed values forward into
	  this image's cache automatically from a bare -D.

	  No default. CMakeLists.txt FATAL_ERRORs at configure time if this
	  is empty or the file isn't there.

config REMOTE_DRV2605_CAL_TEST
	bool "Run a DRV2605L auto-calibration smoke test at boot (bench only)"
	default n
	help
	  Breadboard bring-up for the DRV2605L haptic driver IC on i2c1 (P1.04
	  SDA / P1.05 SCL — remote/boards/nrf52840dk_nrf52840.overlay). Runs
	  drv2605_cal_test_run() before anything else in main(), independent
	  of provisioning/BLE — a bare hardware smoke test that exercises
	  drv2605.c's real driver (drv2605_calibrate()) without needing the
	  dongle, BLE, or the factory link protocol working first, and prints
	  the result and the three per-unit register values (A_CAL_COMP,
	  A_CAL_BEMF, the calibrated FEEDBACK_CONTROL byte) over RTT. Not
	  linked into an ordinary build; src/haptic.c's PWM back end is still
	  what the product path uses until a driver IC decision is made
	  (BUILD_SPEC.md §13).

config REMOTE_SYNTHETIC_VDD_MV
	int "drv2605_read_vdd_mv() placeholder, millivolts (no PMIC on the DK)"
	default 3300
	help
	  There is no nPM1300 on the DK to read a real DRV2605L VDD/VIN
	  voltage from (PLAN.md S17/S18 is where a real fuel gauge arrives).
	  drv2605.c returns this fixed value instead — same convention as
	  link.c's SYNTHETIC_BATTERY_PCT: obviously synthetic rather than a
	  plausible, drifting one.

	  Deliberately defaults BELOW the DRV2605L's 4.0-4.4V OTP-programming
	  window, so drv2605_burn_otp() correctly refuses on every ordinary
	  DK build — there is no real battery here to safely burn OTP
	  against, and refusing is correct, not an inconvenience. Only raise
	  this into the 4.0-4.4V range for a deliberate, supervised bench
	  test of the OTP path itself, on a build nobody mistakes for
	  representative of a real unit's supply.

config REMOTE_TEST_RADIO_PROTO_MAJOR
	int "RR_IDENTITY radio_proto_major to report (bench test only)"
	default 2
	help
	  A14 (RADIO_PROTOCOL.md §14): radio_proto_major has no provisioning-
	  record representation — RP §3.2 fixes it at 2 for this revision
	  (bumped from 1 when DN_INDICATOR's colour field changed shape, RP
	  §16) — so there is no wrong-header way to build the A14 negative
	  case the way A12/A13/A19 are built. This is the one deliberate
	  exception: a bench-only override, defaulting to the real value so
	  an ordinary build is unaffected, set to anything else only for the
	  one negative-case build (PLAN.md queue step S2/S3).

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
